<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

  <!--
    website/views/website_templates.xml emits, unconditionally, inside
    website.layout:

        <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com/" crossorigin=""/>

    Odoo's own comment directly above it is a TODO admitting it should be
    conditional on a Google font actually being used.

    A preconnect is NOT a hint the browser may ignore. Chrome and Firefox both
    open TCP and TLS to fonts.gstatic.com while parsing the head. With the two
    @import lines gone (see primary_variables.scss and fonts.generated.scss)
    that connection carries no request — and it still resolves Google's DNS,
    still exposes every visitor's IP to a third party, still costs a handshake
    on each cold load, and still fails launch gate 6 exactly as written: "no
    request to fonts.gstatic.com on any page".

    Removing the 'url' keys alone therefore does not close gate 6. This does.

    MATCHED ON THE href, NOT ON POSITION. The surrounding block gains and loses
    <link> elements across Odoo point releases, and an xpath anchored to a
    sibling index would start deleting the wrong element rather than failing.
    If Odoo moves or renames this, the upgrade fails loudly with
    "Element ... cannot be located in parent view" — which is the correct
    outcome. A view that silently matches nothing is a gate that silently stops
    being checked.
  -->
  <template id="no_google_font_preconnect"
            inherit_id="website.layout"
            name="MODRYN: no third-party font preconnect">
    <xpath expr="//link[@rel='preconnect'][@href='https://fonts.gstatic.com/']"
           position="replace"/>
  </template>

  <!--
    MODRYN, BESIDE THE BOUTIQUE'S OWN NAME.

    The shop's logo is the shop's - a bride is at Bella Bridal, not at a
    platform - so this sits AFTER it, small, in the gold, and reads as a
    maker's mark rather than a second brand competing with the first.

    BEFORE the shop's logo and not after it, which on a right-to-left page
    puts it hard against the right edge - the first thing on the line.

    A WORDMARK AND NOT AN IMAGE. There is no logo file anywhere in this
    repository; MODRYN is set as letterspaced capitals in the display face, on
    the platform's own site and here. Text scales, prints, reads at any size,
    survives a dark background, and needs no asset to keep in step with the
    other one.
  -->
  <template id="header_modryn_mark" inherit_id="website.option_header_brand_logo"
            name="MODRYN: the platform's mark beside the shop's">
    <!-- Matched on data-name and NOT on hasclass: the parent is an
         INHERIT view, so its arch holds the element as it is written
         there - class comes from t-attf-class, which hasclass() cannot
         see, and the upgrade failed loudly saying so. -->
    <xpath expr="//a[@data-name='Navbar Logo']" position="before">
      <span class="modryn_by">
        <span class="modryn_by_mark">MODRYN</span>
      </span>
    </xpath>
  </template>

</odoo>
